# ─── Snowplow Console (server-only — Signals Node SDK / Signals Inspector) ───
# From Console → API keys. Used by src/lib/signals-server.ts.
SNOWPLOW_CONSOLE_API_KEY_ID=[YOUR-CONSOLE-API-KEY-ID]
SNOWPLOW_CONSOLE_API_KEY=[YOUR-CONSOLE-API-KEY]
SNOWPLOW_CONSOLE_ORG_ID=[YOUR-CONSOLE-ORG-ID]

# ─── Snowplow Signals API host (per-pipeline) ───────────────────────────────
# Default is the sales `prod1` pipeline (collector com-snplow-sales-aws-prod1) —
# the pipeline that hosts the shared `snowplow_id_retrieval` service the Signals
# Inspector uses. Keep this if the demo runs on the sales collector; change only
# if the demo points at a different pipeline.
# Server-side (Signals Node SDK). Either name is accepted by signals-server.ts.
SIGNALS_API_URL=https://7f9742b834d7.signals.snowplowanalytics.com
# Browser-exposed copy — the interventions SSE host for the Signals browser plugin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SNOWPLOW_SIGNALS_API_URL=https://7f9742b834d7.signals.snowplowanalytics.com

# ─── Signals Inspector: Warehouse tab identity gate (MOCK mode only) ─────────
# When siteConfig.warehouse.source === "mock" AND warehouse.identityGate is true,
# the Inspector's "Warehouse" tab stays greyed until the snowplow_id resolved in
# the Identities section exactly equals this value. Set it to the snowplow_id you
# expect your demo persona to resolve to. Leave blank to keep the tab locked.
# Ignored entirely when source === "service".
NEXT_PUBLIC_WAREHOUSE_UNLOCK_SNOWPLOW_ID=

# ─── Nano Banana image generation ───────────────────────────────────────────
# API key for generating demo imagery.
NANOBANANA_API_KEY=[YOUR-NANOBANANA-API-KEY]

# ─── TypeSafe (Jev) — Signals Inspector "Intent" tab ────────────────────────
# Server-only. Powers POST /api/intent, which asks TypeSafe's Jev model for a
# purchase-intent read on the shopper's session state.
#
# TWO names are accepted, and the route checks them in this order:
#   • TYPESAFE_JEV_API_KEY — the name THIS project uses. Set this one.
#   • TYPESAFE_API_KEY     — the name the @typesafe-ai/sdk reads from the
#                            environment by default, kept as a fallback so a
#                            stock SDK setup also works.
# The route resolves the key itself and passes it to `new TypeSafeClient({ apiKey })`,
# so it never depends on the SDK's own env lookup.
#
# With neither set (or with the placeholder below left in place) /api/intent
# returns `configured: false` and the Intent tab shows a "not configured"
# state — the app still builds and runs. Gate the tab with
# siteConfig.features.intent.
TYPESAFE_JEV_API_KEY=[YOUR-TYPESAFE-API-KEY]
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=[YOUR-TYPESAFE-API-KEY]
